<title>USA: Coca-Cola boldly goes brighter --NYT.</title>
<headline>Coca-Cola boldly goes brighter --NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coca-Cola Co has quietly changed the design of its distinctive cans and bottles, The New York Times reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bolder, brighter design has been introduced in Atlanta, Chicago, New York and other cities, and will replace the current cans and bottles throughout the United States and in most other countries in the next two months, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The shape of the cans will not change until Coke decides to introduce the contour cans it has been testing in Europe, it added.</p>
</text>
